(`semantique-team/moth-cs`). The file is reproduced here unchanged to pin the
LM/decoder piece IDs (sha256 `d6e1054e9273915db4e706898286f90d4b97e6b703386ed8b84f0a148caed2fd`).

## Planned data and TTS sources (to be listed when actually used)

Training data must remain commercially usable:

- Common Voice IT 27 (CC0), MLS Italian (CC-BY 4.0), LibriSpeech
  train-clean-100/360 (CC-BY 4.0), and the recorded moth-cs data (CC BY 4.0,
  with consent).
- TTS augmentation with commercially permissive voices: Piper
  `it_IT-paola-medium` (dataset CC0; fine-tuned from the `hifi_tts_92` base model,
  trained on Hi-Fi TTS, CC BY 4.0 — attribute), `it_IT-serena-high` (CC BY 4.0;
  trained on `committa/serena-synthetic-it-27h` by Marco Baccarani, synthetic),
  public-domain English voices such as `en_US-ljspeech-high`, or Kokoro-82M
  (Apache 2.0, Italian voices `if_sara`/`im_nicola`; its training data includes
  synthetic audio from closed TTS providers). No voice cloning of S1/S2/S3.
- Pseudo-labelling candidates: NVIDIA Parakeet-TDT-0.6B-v3 as the teacher
  (CC-BY-4.0); VoxPopuli audio (CC0; © European Union – Source: European
  Parliament).
- CS-FLEURS and SwitchLingua are CC-BY-NC: evaluation only, never training.
  Their use must be stated in the model card and paper. SwitchLingua's agreement
  also forbids commercial applications without the authors' written permission.

Every source and voice licence must be checked again when the data are actually
added; this list is a plan, not a licence audit (the 2026-11-17 check is in
`docs/review-2026-11-17.md` §7).
